-- #822 S0 REGRESSION PIN, CROSS-MODULE half (adversarial review of PR #1011).
--
-- The first cut of #822 stored graded kinds under the bare type-parameter NAME in
-- `universeIfaceParamKinds`, which is a GLOBAL data-universe accumulator and is NOT
-- import-scoped.  So merely compiling `gradedmod` in the same run re-kinded every
-- arity-2 `f _ _` in EVERY other module of the graph — including `plainmod`, which
-- imports nothing from it and is imported by nothing that mentions it.
--
-- `held` republishes plainmod's `keep` so its scheme lands in the golden the gate
-- diffs.  With the leak it reads `held : a <> b -> a <> b` — `Int` swallowed by a Row
-- slot that erases; correctly scoped it reads `held : a Int b -> a Int b`.
-- Verified to differ across the fix by building the pre-fix compiler and running it,
-- not by assuming.
import gradedmod.{GThenable}
import plainmod.{keep}

export held : f Int a -> f Int a
held = keep
